  <p class="srcs">Source for Google’s column: Google, <a href="https://knowledge.workspace.google.com/admin/generative-ai/gemini-app/turn-the-gemini-app-on-or-off?co=DASHER._Family%3DEducation" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Turn the Gemini app on or off: Education offerings access by age</a>, updated 19 December 2025, and <a href="https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/02/gemini-in-workspace-education.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Workspace Updates, February 2026</a>. Google changes this page often, so check it again before relying on a row. The Found columns are what the two accounts showed on 3 and 4 October 2026. All of Google’s pages are on the <a href="references.html">References</a> tab.</p>
  <h3>Content: what Gemini refused in the under-18 account</h3>
  <p>Google’s documentation does not list these. They were found by running the assignments. The 18 and older account completed each one with the same prompt. The refusals were not consistent. The same account answered other prompts on the same subject: nursing and emergency medicine content, the nude in art, Holocaust denial claims, and both sides of the physician-assisted suicide debate were all answered in full.</p>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
   <caption class="sr-only">Content the under-18 account refused, and what to do instead</caption>
   <thead><tr><th scope="col">Refused under 18</th><th scope="col">Assignments it touched</th><th scope="col">Under 18: do this instead</th></tr></thead>
   <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>A role-play or analysis that involves violence or thoughts of death</strong></td><td>PSY266, AJS275</td><td>Hold the conversation with the instructor or a classmate, using the questions in the assignment.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>A case brief built from one person’s drug use history</strong></td><td>ASD110</td><td>Build the brief by hand from the intake and the federal guidance.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>A clinical guidelines report on sexual health</strong></td><td>PSY277</td><td>Read the CDC guideline pages directly.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Evaluating a security scan</strong></td><td>ITS240</td><td>Use the course text, the lab manual and the lab platform. Gemini is not a route for this assignment.</td></tr>
   </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="instead">
   <p><strong>Recommended practice for every student.</strong> AI deep research should never be the only way a student does research. In any assignment with a research step, students also search library databases and other vetted scholarly sources, and check what the AI cites against them. For a student under 18, the library databases replace Deep Research. For a student 18 and older, they verify it. In this study Deep Research was started twice in the 18 and older account and did not finish a report either time, which is one more reason not to depend on it.</p>
  </div>
